Answers files for the unattended installer.

Each file is one machine's install: KEY=value lines that the installer reads line
by line (k_answers_load_env_file in the installer library). It is NOT sourced as
shell: no export, no $VARIABLES, and comments only on their own line. A comment
after a value on the same line is refused. TEMPLATE.env is the complete,
commented reference; start every file from it.

Two ways one reaches a machine:

  USB      ./deploy.sh seed-disk --answers <file> --device /dev/sdX
           writes a 32 MB FAT32 volume labelled KLDLOADSEED holding
           answers.env. kldload-autoinstall finds it by label.

  Netboot  kldload-netboot-server arm-install <mac> <file> serves the file over
           HTTP and puts its URL on that machine's kernel cmdline as
           kldload.seed=http://host/answers/<mac>.env — checked BEFORE the
           seed disk, because a cmdline is per-boot intent and a forgotten
           stick in the front panel is not. Arming checks the file with the
           installer's own loader and refuses what the installer would refuse.

KLDLOAD_DISK may be left empty only on a machine with exactly one candidate:
autoinstall takes the single empty disk, or the disk holding nothing but a
previous kldload install, and refuses to guess between two. Set it explicitly
everywhere else.
